        "deckCaption": "5 diet myths keeping you stuck. And what actually works.\n\nDiet advice online has never been louder. On Reddit, \"Why are Americans so obsessed with not eating seed oils?\" pulled 462 upvotes and 723 comments, and \"What is FINALLY working for me - skipping breakfast!!\" hit 887. Here's what the research actually says.\n\nSources:\n1. 15 controlled trials: adding linoleic acid did not raise inflammation markers. J Acad Nutr Diet, 2012. doi:10.1016/j.jand.2012.03.029\n2. Higher linoleic acid levels linked to lower cardiovascular death in 68,659 people across 30 studies. Circulation, 2019. doi:10.1161/CIRCULATIONAHA.118.038908\n3. Eating breakfast: 260 more calories a day and no extra weight loss across 13 trials. BMJ, 2019. doi:10.1136/bmj.l42\n4. 3 meals vs 6 at the same calories: no difference in fat loss or appetite over 8 weeks. Br J Nutr, 2010. doi:10.1017/S0007114509992984\n5. Low-carb vs low-fat in 609 adults: 6.0 vs 5.3 kg lost after 12 months, and insulin did not predict results. JAMA, 2018. doi:10.1001/jama.2018.0245\n6. At equal calories, cutting fat lost more body fat than cutting carbs (89 vs 53 g a day). Cell Metab, 2015. doi:10.1016/j.cmet.2015.07.021\n7. Eating later raised hunger and lowered waking energy burn. Cell Metab, 2022. doi:10.1016/j.cmet.2022.09.007\n8. Raising protein from 15% to 30% of calories cut intake by 441 calories a day. Am J Clin Nutr, 2005. doi:10.1093/ajcn.82.1.41\n9. Ultra-processed diet: 508 more calories a day eaten, and weight gain. Cell Metab, 2019. doi:10.1016/j.cmet.2019.05.008\n\nThe seed oil heart finding is observational, so it shows a link, not proof.\n\nSave this before your next grocery run. And send it to the friend who still eats 6 meals out of tupperware.\n\nComment MACROS and I'll send you my free macro calculator. And follow @gainsfromgeebs for more myths, checked.\n\n#fitness #nutrition #mythbusting #fatloss #mensfitness #science #gainsfromgeebs",
